# ——— build & deps
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/

# ——— macOS / Google Drive noise
# NOTE: the usual macOS `Icon?` line is deliberately ABSENT. On a
# case-insensitive filesystem it matches `public/icons/` and silently excludes
# every app icon — the PWA then installs on his phone with no home-screen icon,
# and nothing warns you. check-before-publish.sh asserts the icons are tracked.
.DS_Store
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
*.local

# ——— NEVER COMMIT
# This repository is PUBLIC and contains the app ONLY.
#
# `docs/` and `backend/` are deliberately NOT part of it: they carry his real
# spending figures, his name, and family context. Do not copy them in "for
# completeness" — scripts/check-before-publish.sh fails the commit if you do.
#
# The Apps Script endpoint is `Anyone`-accessible by design, so the SECRET is the
# only thing between the internet and his finances. It lives in exactly two
# places, neither of them here:
#   1. CONFIG.SECRET inside the Apps Script editor (pasted, never committed)
#   2. the installed app's localStorage (pasted once via SetupView)
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.secret
secrets.json
